factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 6 problems
  The article says the protest was organized by Vishwa Hindu Parishad, but the reel_script attributes the accusations to 'அமைப்பின் நிர்வாகி' (organisation administrator) without a clear basis; minor, but the article names the speaker only as 'அவர்' (a speaker) and does not identify a role.
  The reel_script says the speaker demanded that persons with two mobile-phone-in-prison cases should not get parole ('பரோல் வழங்கக் கூடாது'); the article says such persons should not have been granted parole, which is roughly consistent, but the reel_script also omits that the speaker criticised the Dravidian parties and TVK government, a key point of the article.
  The reel_script states the 5 persons were released on parole 'கோவையில்' and that the protest was 'நேற்று' - the article says the protest was held yesterday, which is consistent, but the reel_script's first sentence places the parole in Coimbatore, which the article does not state.
  The reel_script and slides omit the article's central claim that the Dravidian parties were responsible for the lack of action on the blast and that the TVK government made a historic mistake; the caption also omits it.
  The slide title 'அமைப்பின்' is an incomplete/ungrammatical heading with no clear meaning in Tamil.
  The caption says the speaker 'கோரினார்/ தவறை சரி செய்யாவிட்டால் பெரிய தவறாகும் என்றும், இதை முதல்வர் முடிவு செய்ய வேண்டும் என்றும்' merges two different demands (correcting the mistake and the Chief Minister deciding on TVK) into one sentence, mixing two facts.
